WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
We begin in the existing
FireSat system model.

2
00:00:03.243 --> 00:00:06.480 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Asset identification is an input to SSTPA:

3
00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:10.380 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
the team has already decided that
authentic fire reports matter

4
00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:11.180 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
to the mission.

5
00:00:11.540 --> 00:00:15.300 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Here we record that protection
decision in a separate tutorial asset,

6
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.940 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
without changing the original example asset.

7
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:23.040 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
In Asset Manager, choose New Asset
and enter FireSat tutorial reports.

8
00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.580 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Keep the asset type Organic,
select Mission Critical,

9
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.260 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
and select Authenticity.

10
00:00:28.609 --> 00:00:32.220 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
These choices state why the reports
matter and which property this

11
00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.420 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
analysis will protect.

12
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:36.340 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
They do not establish that
protection has succeeded.

13
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.880 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
For Environment, choose
Payload Operating Environment.

14
00:00:40.033 --> 00:00:43.780 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Select Create, with Losses and
Goals automatically generated.

15
00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:47.580 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This saves the new asset and
its associated analysis records.

16
00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:51.240 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Selecting the environment here completes
the context that would otherwise

17
00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:53.300 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
need assignment through the Context Tool.

18
00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:57.880 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Find the generated entry under Loss
nodes and choose Open in Loss Tool.

19
00:00:58.022 --> 00:01:01.580 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Use Selected Loss to choose
the tutorial record explicitly;

20
00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:05.620 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
opening the tool does not guarantee
that it selected the intended Loss.

21
00:01:05.751 --> 00:01:09.140 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Check the Asset, Environment,
and Criticality and Assurance

22
00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:10.560 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
fields before continuing.

23
00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.680 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
The root expresses the
compromise we will investigate:

24
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:17.160 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
fire reports whose claimed
origin cannot be trusted.

25
00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:21.960 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
In SSTPA, Loss measures the effort an
attacker needs to expend to violate

26
00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:25.140 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
one Assurance on one
asset in one environment.

27
00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:27.860 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
Building the supporting
attack structure comes next.

28
00:01:28.062 --> 00:01:31.840 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
At the upper right of the canvas,
select Nocturne for dark mode,

29
00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:33.420 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
then Parchment to return.

30
00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.480 line:92% position:50% size:94% align:center
This changes presentation only.
